# implementation_plan_phase12.md

# Phase 12: The Critic Loop (Self-Evolution)

## Goal
To implement the "Critic Loop" described in Nucleus Vision, enabling the system to self-correct code before asking for human review.

> **Vision Ref:** "Phase 3: Team of Teams... The Critic Loop: Coder writes -> Reviewer critiques -> Coder fixes."

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This phase will introduce *automatic code modification* based on LLM critique. We will start with a "Suggest Only" mode before enabling "Auto-Apply".

## Proposed Changes

### 1. The Persona (New)
#### [NEW] [.brain/agents/critic.md](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/.gemini/antigravity/brain/7c654df4-b83e-43f9-8620-f15868ec39d1/.brain/agents/critic.md)
- Define the "Senior Reviewer" persona.
- **Capabilities**: Read code, Linting (if available), Static Analysis (Regex).
- **Style**: Ruthless, security-focused, best-practice oriented.

### 2. The Tools (New)
#### [MODIFY] [mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py)
- `brain_critique_code(file_path: str, context: str) -> str`:
    - Reads file.
    - Sends to LLM with "Critic" system prompt.
    - Returns structured critique (Issues, Severity, Suggestion).
- `brain_apply_critique(file_path: str, critique_id: str) -> str`:
    - Takes a specific critique and applies the fix (Concept/Placeholder for now).

### 3. The Integration (Workflows)
#### [MODIFY] [server.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/server.py)
- Add `POST /api/critique` endpoint to trigger a review on a specific file via the HUD.

#### [MODIFY] [ResearchWidget.tsx](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/ResearchWidget.tsx)
- Rename to "OperationsWidget"?
- Add "Code Review" tab/button to trigger critique on active file.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Create [tests/test_critic_loop.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tests/test_critic_loop.py):
    1. Create a "bad" python file (syntax error or bad practice).
    2. Call `brain_critique_code`.
    3. Assert the response identifies the error.

### Manual Verification
- Use the HUD to trigger a critique on [server.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/orchestrator_server.py) itself.
- Verify the "Critic" speaks via TTS (Mission 4 Integration).
